# /etc/rc - commands the init shell reads once, before the first prompt.
#
# The syntax is the console's, because it is the same parser: one command per
# line, '#' starts a comment, a trailing '&' backgrounds a command, blank
# lines are ignored.  `exit N` ends the script with code N instead of
# shutting the machine down.
#
# `source <file>` runs another script in this process; `run sh <file>` runs
# one as a separate task (a new pid, a new window - and the C3 has only three
# windows in total, so prefer source for anything that runs a program).
#
# This file is empty on purpose.  A boot that talks without being asked is a
# boot you cannot diff, and every byte printed here lands in front of each
# acceptance test and smoke run.  Uncomment to taste:
#
# echo [rc] hello from the boot script
# uptime
